<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 55.3 trln lira of 2-yr bonds.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 55.3 trln lira of 2-yr bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury sold 55.3 trillion lira of two-year, inflation-indexed bonds at 29.95 percent risk premium on Tuesday, compared to 34.6 trillion lira sale and 25 percent risk premium in the previous auction on May 6.</p>
<p>Results on page  CBTI.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : May 14, 1999</p>
<p>	Amount			: 55.27 trln lira</p>
<p>	Bid amount		  : 69.7  trln lira</p>
<p>	Risk premium		: 29.95 percent</p>
<p>	Payment date		: May 14, 1997</p>
<p>There will be three-month coupon payments on the bonds.</p>
<p>Banks will pay 54.7 trillion lira for the auction on Wednesday when the treasury faces 78.2 trillion lira of repayments for maturing bills.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
